course: dictionary
lesson: 10893
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Viral» is one of these words. In «a viral infection», it means caused by a virus, such as a cold or flu.
explain: Online, «viral» has a newer meaning. When a video «goes viral», it spreads very fast because huge numbers of people share it. Clues such as online, shared or millions tell you this is the meaning to choose.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. «The video went viral» makes sense with spread very fast. It would not make sense to say the video was caused by a virus.
fact: Viral means caused by a virus.
fact: «A viral infection» is an illness caused by a virus, such as a cold or flu.
fact: «Going viral» means spreading very fast online, as millions of people share something.
fact: Antibiotics do not work on viral illnesses, but washing your hands helps stop viruses spreading.
fact: Before you share a viral story, ask who says so, and whether it could be fake.
exercise: «She caught a viral infection and stayed in bed for a week.» What does viral mean here? | Spread very fast online | *Caused by a virus | Coloured green or yellow | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «The funny clip went viral in one afternoon.» What does went viral mean? | Was lost forever | Was made by a famous singer | *Spread very fast as many people shared it | Was checked by a doctor
exercise: Why do antibiotics not help with a viral cold? | Antibiotics only work on people over 10 | Colds are always caused by sunshine | *Antibiotics do not work on viruses
test: Before you share a viral picture, what should you ask? | How many likes does it need? | Is it a nice colour? | *Who says so, and is it real or edited?
test: Which words in «The viral video was shared by millions» tell you it spread widely? | The viral video | Was the video | *Shared by millions
exam: «Such viral scares are usually hoaxes.» What does viral mean here? | *Spreading very fast, often across the internet | Caused by a virus | Shown only on television | Written in a secret code
